# 0003. The repo is the live config, one config for macOS and Arch

- Status: Accepted
- Date: 2026-11-05

## Context
The same editor is used on a Mac and an Arch desktop and should behave the same on both.

## Decision
- `~/.config/nvim` is a symlink to this repo (`make link`; an existing config is moved to
  `~/.config/nvim.bak-<date>`, never deleted; `make unlink` restores it).
- One config for both OSes; differences go through `vim.fn.has("mac")` checks
  (e.g. `detect_os` in `ui.lua`), not separate branches or files.
- `make install` sets up a machine: tools (pacman / brew / apt / dnf), link, plugins, servers.
- Changes go through branches and PRs; `main` is what every machine runs.

## Alternatives
Not recorded at the time.

## Rationale
One source of truth; `git pull && make sync` brings a machine up to date.

## Consequences
- The checked-out branch is the editor in use right now: a feature branch left checked out is
  live, and never reaches the other machine. Switch back to `main` after pushing.

## References
- `Makefile`, `scripts/install-tools.sh`, `CLAUDE.md`
